ce therapy [Data: Relationships (19997, 20001); Entities (1075, 2328)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Clinical monitoring of 收缩压 is critical during therapy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Multiple formulations of 单硝酸异山梨酯—包括 缓释胶囊Ⅱ, 胶, and the base compound—are explicitly linked to effects on 收缩压 (systolic blood pressure). Clinical guidance consistently warns that in patients with low filling pressures (e.g., post-acute myocardial infarction), systolic blood pressure should not fall below 90 mmHg. This necessitates careful hemodynamic monitoring during treatment initiation or dose adjustment. The repeated appearance of this caution across structured sources highlights a standardized safety protocol tied to this drug class [Data: Relationships (1104, 1105, 1106); Entities (13580)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Associated symptoms reflect underlying cardiovascular pathology\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Symptoms such as 气短 (shortness of breath), 乏力 (fatigue), and 心肌梗死 (myocardial infarction) appear in the network as manifestations of the diseases treated by 单硝酸异山梨酯 or as potential adverse outcomes. For example, 慢性充血性心力衰竭 is documented to present with 气短 and 乏力, while 心肌梗死 itself is listed as both an indication context and a symptom entity. Although no direct relationship links 单硝酸异山梨酯 to causing 心肌梗死, its use in post-infarction care situates it within this clinical landscape [Data: Entities (18189, 18075, 1075); Relationships (18110, 18026)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses moderate-to-high clinical impact due to the serious adverse reactions and significant drug–drug interactions associated with widely used cardiovascular medications.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 178212